GE OF SURGEONS:The American College of Surgeons is a professional organization that evaluates patient care and outcomes in surgical practices, including esophageal cancer.", "CANCER CACHEXIA:Cancer cachexia is a complex syndrome that significantly impacts cancer patients, characterized by severe body weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and alterations in metabolism. This condition often involves not only the loss of muscle but also fat, leading to a notable decline in overall body composition. It is frequently observed in patients with advanced stages of cancer, particularly those suffering from pancreatic and esophageal cancers. The syndrome is associated with decreased appetite, which further exacerbates the nutritional challenges faced by these patients. Due to its profound effects on health and quality of life, cancer cachexia has become a significant focus of research within the field of oncology, highlighting the need for specialized nutritional interventions and support to manage this debilitating condition effectively.", "SERUM C-REACTIVE PROTEIN:Serum C-reactive protein is a marker that is studied in relation to prognosis in esophageal carcinoma.", "GLASGOW PROGNOSTIC SCORE:The Glasgow Prognostic Score is a clinical tool used to predict outcomes in cancer patients, particularly those with esophageal cancer.", "PREOPERATIVE WEIGHT LOSS:Preoperative weight loss is a condition studied in relation to postoperative outcomes in esophageal cancer patients.", "POSTOPERATIVE COURSE:Postoperative course refers to the recovery process following surgery, particularly in esophageal cancer resection.", "NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY:Neoadjuvant chemotherapy is a treatment given before surgery to shrink tumors, often used in patients with esophageal cancer to improve surgical outcomes.", "CRITICAL REVIEWS IN ONCOLOGY HEMATOLOGY:Critical Reviews in Oncology Hematology is a journal that publishes reviews on various aspects of oncology and hematology, including cancer cachexia an